{
 "name": "log-core",
 "description": "Structured log, core: log_put / log_chg / log_cnt write 16-byte records {u16 id, u16 sequence, u32 time, u32 arg0, u32 arg1} into one RAM ring per CPU (512 records each, in RAM that no load or clear touches, 0x7E4F9000-0x7E4FD2C0 through the uncached alias). They never call the file system. Events: boot, firmware error (the recorder 0x7E426D4B), GUI state. The dormant task USRTEST_A becomes the flush task: when the GUI enters a menu, playback or power-off state and the card is not being written, it appends the new records to C:\\EPM2LOG.BIN in 512-byte blocks (stops at 4 MiB). DEBUG builds only. The event ids are in data/logdict/events.json (build id d1ddd46b4dac2414). A delta on data/builds/peaking-colours.json: every expect is a byte string of that build. See experiments/2026-11-15-log/NOTES.md and docs/reference/logging.md.",
